  "subject": "🏞️ Axios Finish Line: Prescribing nature",
  "date": "Wed, 04 Nov 2026 21:29:43 -0500",
  "body_text": "96 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n 📻 Plus: Kindness via boombox | Wednesday, November 04, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n View in browser \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n Axios Finish Line \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n By Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei &middot; Nov 04, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n Welcome back! Smart Brevity™ count: 386 words … 1½ mins. Edited by Natalie Daher and copy edited by Amy Stern. \n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 1 big thing — Your next Rx: Nature \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Illustration: Natalie Peeples/Axios\n\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n A prescription for birdwatching? Doctor's orders to do some gardening?\n\n It might not be as far-fetched as it sounds. A new study co-authored by University of Colorado Boulder researchers suggests that spending time in nature can fight loneliness — even if you go it alone, Axios Denver's Alayna Alvarez reports. Why it matters: With 1 in 6 people worldwide experiencing loneliness, researchers are looking for remedies that go beyond traditional medical care.\n\n 🔬 Zoom in: The study, published last month in The Lancet Regional Health , followed 320 adults experiencing loneliness in Barcelona.\n\n Half participated in weekly two-hour group outings to parks and gardens and other nature-based activities for nine weeks. The rest received recommendations for free, accessible outdoor activities they could do on their own. What they found: Loneliness scores dropped an average of 10.5% after three months and nearly 17% after a year across both groups.\n\n Group outings were especially effective for participants who started out lonelier or with poorer emotional well-being. But both groups reported feeling less lonely, whether exploring nature together or alone. 🍂 What's next: CU Boulder professor Jill Litt, who led the international research project behind the study, notes that research on how nature can combat loneliness could lead to new programs.\n\n That could mean group outings in parks as an accessible, affordable form of therapy, or insurance coverage for activities like joining birdwatching clubs. Share this story ... Find your Axios Local city . \n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\nA MESSAGE FROM AXIOS\r\n\n \r\n See what's next for media in 2027 \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n Media Trends Executive Annual members receive the 2026 Annual Report, our special media document featuring global forecasts, sector analysis and exclusive media data insights.\r\n\n\r\n \r\n🔒 Get the report by becoming a Media Trends Executive member.\r\n\n\r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 2. 🚲 Spreading joy \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Stock: Getty Images\n\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Joy du jour from reader Claire Duchene of Brooklyn, N.Y.:\n\n \"Lately, I've taken up cycling in Prospect Park. The other day I was on a ride, and a man was blasting music from his boombox and dancing for the amusement of all passing cyclists and runners. At first, with my headphones on, I did what most New Yorkers would do and ignored the man.\" \"On my second pass, I paid more attention and couldn't help but smile at his infectious enthusiasm, dance moves and cheering of the passing runners, a few of whom danced and jammed along with him as they passed. ... That stranger made my day with his expression of pure joy and desire to share it with the world.\" \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n 🏁 Please invite your friends to join Finish Line . \n\n \r\n 👆 Like this comms style and format? It's called Smart Brevity®. Bring it to your org — via hands-on training or internal comms software — to harness its power and impact. \r\n &nbsp; Axios thanks our partners for supporting our journalism.\n Advertise with us. \n\n Read more about Axios' mission , ethics and how we use AI in our journalism . You can reach the authors by replying to this email.\nSponsorship has no influence on editorial content.\n\n Thank you for signing up for this Axios newsletter. To stop receiving this newsletter, unsubscribe or manage your email preferences . If someone forwarded this to you, sign up now to get Axios in your inbox.\n\n Axios, PO Box 101060, Arlington VA 22201 &nbsp; Follow Axios across:\n\n &nbsp; &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;",
