03c94aB9ea87461\"><img src=\"https://link.axios.com/img/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94asqgoq.94gf/2b54c743.gif\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\" /></a></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding-right:3.5%\" align=\"right\"> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48263930.425679/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL25ld3NsZXR0ZXJzL2F4aW9zLWZpbmlzaC1saW5lLThhZWRmM2U2LTIxMjctNDFmMy1hOTkyLWNiZDZkYTc0OTBmZi5odG1sP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB24cd184b\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"b\" style=\"color:#222;font-size:13px;font-family:'gordita',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;text-decoration:underline\">View in browser</a> </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td height=\"30\" style=\"height:30px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>  <tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1.3\"> </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td height=\"16\" style=\"height:16px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1\">\r\n<span class=\"s\" style=\"font-size:44px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#008dc8;letter-spacing:-1px;line-height:1\"> Axios Finish Line </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1.5;padding-bottom:35px;padding-top:10px\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#222;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">By  Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei  <span style=\"margin:0 6px\">&middot;</span> Nov 04, 2026 </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;line-height:1.75;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;padding:0 3.5%\"><p><strong>Welcome back! </strong><em>Smart Brevity™ count: 386 words … 1½ mins. Edited by Natalie Daher and copy edited by Amy Stern.</em></p></td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">   1 big thing — Your next Rx: Nature </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td> <img src=\"https://images.axios.com/qkeS9g2UQe_CwsDQRuF5egIdXa8=/1920x1080/smart/2024/03/14/200241-1710446561489.jpg\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" id=\"item02\" alt=\"Illustration of a pile of dirt with a heart shaped plant sprouting from it.\"> </td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.3\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#848484\"> <p>Illustration: Natalie Peeples/Axios</p> </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><p><strong>A prescription for birdwatching? </strong>Doctor's orders to do some gardening?</p><ul><li><strong>It might not be</strong> as far-fetched as it sounds. A <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48263930.425679/aHR0cHM6Ly9kb2kub3JnLzEwLjEwMTYvai5sYW5lcGUuMjAyNi4xMDE4MjE_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB4a761e1e\" target=\"_blank\">new study</a> co-authored by University of Colorado Boulder researchers suggests that spending time in nature can fight loneliness — even if you go it alone, <em>Axios Denver's Alayna Alvarez reports.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Why it matters: </strong>With <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48263930.425679/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cud2hvLmludC90ZWFtcy9zb2NpYWwtZGV0ZXJtaW5hbnRzLW9mLWhlYWx0aC9kZW1vZ3JhcGhpYy1jaGFuZ2UtYW5kLWhlYWx0aHktYWdlaW5nL3NvY2lhbC1pc29sYXRpb24tYW5kLWxvbmVsaW5lc3M_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB7be3f4ea\" target=\"_blank\">1 in 6 people worldwide</a> experiencing loneliness, researchers are looking for remedies that go beyond traditional medical care.</p><p>🔬 <strong>Zoom in: </strong>The study, published last month in <em>The Lancet Regional Health</em>, followed 320 adults experiencing loneliness in Barcelona.</p><ul><li><strong>Half participated</strong> in weekly two-hour group outings to parks and gardens and other nature-based activities for nine weeks.</li><li><strong>The rest received </strong>recommendations for free, accessible outdoor activities they could do on their own.</li></ul><p><strong>What they found: </strong>Loneliness scores dropped an average of 10.5% after three months and nearly 17% after a year across both groups.</p><ul><li><strong>Group outings </strong>were especially effective for participants who started out lonelier or with poorer emotional well-being. But both groups reported feeling less lonely, whether exploring nature together or alone.</li></ul><p><strong>🍂 What's next: </strong>CU Boulder professor Jill Litt, who led the international research project behind the study, <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48263930.425679/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuY29sb3JhZG8uZWR1L3RvZGF5LzIwMjYvMTAvMTMvY2FuLXByZXNjcmlwdGlvbi1uYXR1cmUtaGVscC1jdXJlLWxvbmVsaW5lc3MtZXBpZGVtaWM_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB26cfc7b4\" target=\"_blank\">notes</a> that research on how nature can combat loneliness could lead to new programs.</p><ul><li><strong>That could mean </strong>group outings in parks as an accessible, affordable form of therapy, or insurance coverage for activities like joining birdwatching clubs.</li></ul><p><em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48263930.425679/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL2xvY2FsL2RlbnZlci8yMDI2LzEwLzIzL2N1LWJvdWxkZXItc3R1ZHktbmF0dXJlLXByZXNjcmlwdGlvbi1sb25lbGluZXNzP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB3c8308e7\" target=\"_blank\">Share this story</a> ... <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48263930.425679/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL25ld3NsZXR0ZXJzL2xvY2FsP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB49eacc71\" target=\"_blank\">Find your Axios Local city</a>.</em></p></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48263930.425679/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtZmluaXNoLWxpbmUtOGFlZGYzZTYtMjEyNy00MWYzLWE5OTItY2JkNmRhNzQ5MGZmLmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0QxJTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3RvcnkxJnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBfc9fb7ff\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48263930.425679/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9pbnRlbnQvdHdlZXQ_\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-x-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Tweet this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48263930.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.co